<td style="font-variant:small-caps; font-size:0.95em; padding-bottom:9px"><b> The Luminous Fairies and Mothra | BOOK REVIEW </b>
</td></tr></tbody></table>
<p><big><b>The Luminous Fairies and Mothra | BOOK REVIEW</b> - <a rel="nofollow" class="external text" href="https://youtu.be/O38HIHSlsxA">watch on YouTube</a></big>
</p><p><big>The original <a href="/wiki/1961" title="1961">1961</a> <a href="/wiki/Mothra" title="Mothra">Mothra</a> novella, which introduced the lepidopteran daikaiju, has at long last been translated into English by Jeffrey Angles, who previously translated the <i><a href="/wiki/Godzilla_and_Godzilla_Raids_Again" title="Godzilla and Godzilla Raids Again">Godzilla and Godzilla Raids Again</a></i> novels! Published by the University of Minnesota Press.</big>
</p><p><i>Read more: <a href="/wiki/The_Luminous_Fairies_and_Mothra" title="The Luminous Fairies and Mothra">The Luminous Fairies and Mothra</a></i>
</p><p><br /><script src="https://apis.google.com/js/platform.js"></script>

<div class="g-ytsubscribe" data-channel="GodzillaWiki" data-layout="full" data-count="default"></div>
</p>
